# RaphCare Feature Checklist Updates

Whenever you implement, finish, or materially change a feature on **API**, **Web admin**, **`RaphCare.Client`**, or **Mobile**, **update** `docs/raphcare-feature-checklist.md` in the same change set.

**Always keep a PDF next to the markdown:** `docs/raphcare-feature-checklist.pdf`. Whenever the `.md` changes, regenerate the PDF in the same change set (see below). Do not leave the PDF stale.

## What to update

1. Mark completed items `[x]`.
2. Leave incomplete items `[ ]`.
3. Adjust `(partial)` / `(blocked: …)` / `(out of scope)` notes so they match reality.
4. Set **Last reviewed** to today’s date.
5. If you invent a new feature area, add a checklist row under the right step (admin outpatient, inpatient, patient mobile, or staff APIs).
6. Regenerate **`docs/raphcare-feature-checklist.pdf`** after any markdown edit:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/Export-RaphCareFeatureChecklistPdf.ps1
```

Styles live in `docs/raphcare-feature-checklist.pdf.css`; options in `docs/raphcare-feature-checklist.pdf.json`. Commit the updated `.pdf` with the `.md`.

## Related docs (do not replace the checklist)

- **Mobile visual parity** — `docs/Mobile_Concept_Port.md` (tokens, route map, screen table). Update when concept or MAUI UI changes.
- **Mobile release gates** — `docs/Mobile_Release_Ready_Checklist.md` (flags, quality bar). Update when rollout or cross-cutting readiness changes.
- **Layer order** — backend first, then Client, then Web / Mobile (see **raphcare-solution-layers**).

## Step exit / polish

Treat each numbered step’s remaining open rows as the exit criteria for that step:

- Do not treat a step as done while non-blocked product rows are still `[ ]`.
- For **Mobile** screens, mark checklist / parity done only when the flow is usable **and** matches the concept for spacing, cards, empty states, and branding (see `Mobile_Concept_Port.md`)—not when only a stub or under-construction page exists.
- For **admin Web**, match existing `Pages/Admin/Hospitals/*` patterns (layout, alerts, empty states) in the same change set as the feature wire-up.
- Move an item out of `(blocked: …)` when the API (or Client) now exists and is wired.

## Do / don't

- Do update the checklist when the feature is usable end-to-end on the intended surface(s).
- Do add Client + UI checklist rows when you add a new HTTP contract.
- Don't mark admin or mobile UI done if only the API handler exists.
- Don't skip the checklist update because the code change was “small.”
- Don't invent Mobile admin/inpatient rows unless product explicitly scopes a clinician app (checklist marks those out of scope today).
